  "score": null,
  "definition": "Homoplasmate is PKD's term for the symbiosis of human and plasmate — what Jesus was: \"homo (man); plasmate (Logos)\" (CLM_S_40ace5af19). PKD identifies himself as one — \"Zebra acting in syzygy with a human\" (CLM_S_aa6d7a5835). \"Thomas,\" the apostolic-era figure he believed he had recovered, was \"the homoplasmate which Zebra took over just after the death of Christ\" (CLM_S_4de82fd890).",
  "interpretive_note": "The homoplasmate is PKD's account of how the Logos enters history. The structure is Bob Wilson's \"interspecies symbiosis\": a living info life-form bonds with a human, and the result is what Jesus was — \"homo (man); plasmate (Logos)\" (CLM_S_40ace5af19). PKD claims the same status for himself in 3-74: \"PKD is a homoplasmate: Zebra acting in syzygy with a human\" (CLM_S_aa6d7a5835). The \"Thomas\" identity recovered in his anamnesis was, on this reading, \"the homoplasmate which Zebra took over just after the death of Christ\" — and the bond was severed once before by the killing of those it had bonded with, forcing Zebra to \"short-circuit time\" to reincarnate (CLM_S_4de82fd890, CLM_S_381061c3d5).",
  "visionary_significance": null,
  "scholarly_caution": null,
  "card_description": "A human bonded with the plasmate; PKD believed he became one during 2-3-74.",
  "full_description": "A human bonded with the plasmate; PKD believed he became one during 2-3-74.\n\n**Category:** PKD Visionary",
